 carry over to the next batch, so it spoils. Holding costs are higher, and both products together are near the warehouse limit.\n\n**3. Candidate 0 against candidate 3.** Both order every 2 days and arrive in the same rhythm. The difference is how much spare stock they order.\n- **Product 0:** candidate 0 orders exactly the expected demand (forecast × 1.046), with no spare stock. Candidate 3 orders about 7% more, roughly 3 spare units per 2-day cycle. Demand over 2 days varies by about ±10 units. A missing unit costs 10 (6 lost margin plus a 4 penalty). A spare unit usually just carries into the next cycle for a small holding cost, because the 4-day shelf life covers two cycles.\n- **Product 1:** a missing unit costs 15 (8 margin plus a 7 penalty), and a spare unit costs at most 4 if it spoils. Here too, candidate 3's larger spare stock pays off.\n\n**4. Variability.** When actual demand moves away from the forecast, candidate 3's spare stock absorbs the swings better. It stays well within the warehouse limit (about 90 arriving plus about 20 already on hand)."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3876, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2269, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3876}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T08:06:31.767Z", "request_id": "req_011CgF36HCbNoKzULNXEwGFb"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01JANiMhD6e2yQRZ9Rq45rch", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id":