1 every 4 days, which only adds holding cost.\n\n**Candidate 0 against candidate 3:**\n- Product 0: candidate 0 orders exactly the expected demand (forecast × 1.046). Because leftovers carry over, its stock behaves like a random walk with no upward trend, and shortages are moderate. Candidate 3 orders about 7% more, roughly 3–4 extra units per cycle. That saves about 18 units of shortage (about 180), but about 23 units are never sold (about 230) and holding rises by about 250–300.\n- Product 1: candidate 0 already orders about 14% above expected demand. Candidate 3's extra 25% mostly expires; the shortages it prevents (cost 15 per unit) don't make up for the extra purchase and holding.\n- Neither plan runs short of cash, and the product-1 shortage at the start (no delivery until day 5) is the same for every candidate.\n\n**Uncertainty:** candidates 0 and 3 are close, and random demand could swing the result by about ±200. Candidate 6 is not far behind them either."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 3920, "cache_read_input_tokens": 2304, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 3920}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-21T08:07:55.645Z", "request_id": "req_011CgF3AQmsAdQpa7RVtu9UK"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_0114ZMKuKG84B8xHzcS5hgpi", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgF3ARFQ5gmFY